<%# Where this ONE application stands, at the top of its own page.

   The index answers this for the whole search in three strips, and the page
   actually open while something is being written down answered none of it:
   whose move it is, how deep this went, how many times it has been round and
   whether there is an interview to turn up to all had to be reconstructed by
   reading the timeline underneath.

   Lines first, figures second. A booking to attend and a thing owed are tasks;
   the rest is a read, and it wears the quiet panel the standings table on the
   index wears for the same reason. %>
<%
  latest = job.latest_beat
  # Nothing is owed on an application that is over, and nothing is booked on
  # one either - a rejection clears the calendar (JobNote#withdraw_booking) but
  # the note it cleared is still on the row.
  owed = latest&.owed unless job.dead?
  booked = job.next_interview_at unless job.dead?
  unreported = job.unreported_interview_at unless job.dead?
  # The frame goes to the appointment ahead of the errand, the way the index
  # orders its strips: one of these is a room to be in at a time.
  frame = (booked || unreported ? "is-booked" : ("is-waiting" if owed.present?))
%>
<div class="job-standing <%= frame %>">
  <% if unreported.present? %>
    <div class="standing-step">
      <span class="note-tag note-tag-scheduled">Interview</span>
      <%= interview_day(unreported) %>
      <span class="field-hint">how did it go? Write it up below.</span>
    </div>
  <% elsif booked.present? %>
    <div class="standing-step">
      <span class="note-tag note-tag-scheduled">Interview</span>
      <%= interview_day(booked) %>
    </div>
  <% end %>

  <%# What is owed leads its own line, as it does on the index — the verb is
     the part being scanned for. %>
  <% if owed.present? %>
    <div class="standing-step">
      <span class="standing-owed"><%= owed %></span>
      <span class="field-hint">
        waiting on you &middot; <%= waiting_age(latest.occurred_at) %>
      </span>
    </div>
  <% end %>

  <dl class="standing-facts">
    <div>
      <dt>Reached</dt>
      <dd><%= job.engagement_label || "No reply yet" %></dd>
    </div>

    <div>
      <dt>Interactions</dt>
      <dd><%= job.interaction_count %></dd>
    </div>

    <%# Over is neither move. The status control directly below says which way
       it went, so repeating it here would be the second copy of one fact. %>
    <% unless job.dead? %>
      <div>
        <dt>Move</dt>
        <dd class="<%= "is-yours" if owed.present? %>">
          <%= owed.present? ? "Yours" : "Theirs" %>
        </dd>
      </div>
    <% end %>

    <div>
      <dt>Last beat</dt>
      <dd><%= standing_age(job.engaged_at) %></dd>
    </div>

    <%# Only once he has rated something. An unrated application showing two
       dashes says "there is a thing here you have not done", which is a chore
       on a panel that exists to say where the application stands. %>
    <% job.sentiment.each do |field, score| %>
      <div>
        <dt><%= field == :did_well ? "Did" : "Liked" %></dt>
        <dd title="<%= JobNote::SENTIMENT[field] %>">
          <%= score %><span class="field-hint">/<%= JobNote::SENTIMENT_CEILING %></span>
        </dd>
      </div>
    <% end %>
  </dl>
</div>
